# Fluent Mobile agent instructions (Cursor)

**Shared canon:** root [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) — delivery gates, precedence, ownership, multi-tool discovery. Do not fork those policies here.

**Claude Code** loads [`CLAUDE.md`](../../CLAUDE.md) (which `@` imports `AGENTS.md`). This bridge is the **Cursor** adapter only.

## Reuse (do not duplicate)

- Skills: `.claude/skills/*/SKILL.md`
- Commands / workflows: `.claude/commands/*.md` — **read these files** to run a command
- Review agents: `.claude/agents/*.md` (invoke `code-reviewer` by path)
- PR template: `.cursor/templates/pr-template.md` (GitHub UI mirror `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`) — **one format only**

**Agent models:** repo agents under `.claude/agents/` use `model: inherit` (do not pin model aliases).

When a task matches a skill description, read that `SKILL.md` first.

## Cursor-only facts (not universal)

- **Rules:** `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` — `alwaysApply`, `globs`, or description-based. Claude Code does **not** auto-load these files.
- **Hooks:** `.cursor/hooks.json` — session env + architecture-guard; **warn-only**, never deny tools.
- **Slash-command shims:** `.cursor/commands/*.md` only register names in Cursor’s `/` palette. They are **not** required for the command to work and are **not** documented as Cursor CLI auto-load. Always execute by reading `.claude/commands/<name>.md`. Edit the `.claude` file as the single source of truth; never duplicate logic into the shim.

## Repo workflow (shared)

PRs target `main`. Track work on Project 4 (`Refs #NNN` — never closing keywords; `Refs: none` only for in-session no-ticket chores). See `docs/issue-tracking.md`. Delivery procedure: `.claude/commands/create-pr.md`.

**Global IDE user rules:** if they conflict with this repo, prefer `AGENTS.md`, this file, and the rest of `.cursor/rules/`.
